        "id": "p0",
        "title": "Special Knockdown",
        "text": "Some knockdowns leave the opponent briefly hittable while they're still lying on the floor. Landing a hit in that window is called an off-the-ground hit, or OTG. The knockdown move itself creates that state - you can't turn an ordinary knockdown into an OTG just by picking the right follow-up attack."
      },
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "title": "Mai's OTG Route",
        "text": "Mai's ground throw is the easy example. With RED RF ready, throw from close range with {dir:6}/{dir:4} + {btn:C}, cancel the connected throw with {input:22C}, then press {input:2C}. The IC gets Mai moving again just in time for 2C to catch the grounded window: Throw > IC > 2C."
      }
    ],
    "tasks": [
      {
